 "verdict": "validated",
 "notes": "Validated on all main criteria. Sampled return is 21.96 vs 21.71 (+1.2%), random play is -0.42 / 7.67 steps vs -0.40 / 7.84, and the critic TD residual is 0.0065, against 0.08-1.5 for every structural alternative. Two caveats. (1) The TD residual cannot tell 'catch if paddle under ball OR landing cell' or 'no serve pause' apart from the best rules (0.007-0.011); only the random-play stats separate them (random -0.23 / 9.2 and -0.41 / 6.8 respectively). The 1-step serve pause is indistinguishable from the reference counting one extra step per episode. (2) Our returns are nearly deterministic (2 mirror-image starts), while the reference has sd ~1.11, so the true start set probably has a little more variety (ball start cols 1-8 or a random paddle start made the trained policy lose and broke the random stats). The trained policy also loses very rarely in ours (mean length 199.7), but never in the reference. The corner-catch dx flip is almost never exercised."
}